+## Task 39 (item B-W15) — docs/dev/sync-discipline.md, docs/dev/lens-contribution-policy.md
+
+- **B-W15 correction 3 (wording changed to meet the AC).** Planned: "the JobSpec `custom_prompt_dir` field (a `--custom-prompt-dir` flag is planned, not shipped)". That text contains the literal string the AC requires to be absent (`grep -n -- "--custom-prompt-dir"` returns nothing). Written instead: "the JobSpec `custom_prompt_dir` field (set in the spec file; no `swarm run` option sets it in 5.0.0)". Evidence: `swarm/models.py:115` (`custom_prompt_dir: Optional[str] = None`); no swarm subcommand defines the option (`superclaude swarm run --help`, `swarm --help` command list); `swarm/commands.py:1164-1168` rejects `--lens custom` with "supply a spec file with custom_prompt_dir set instead"; the option is only foreseen in a comment (`swarm/commands.py:123-127`). The `:234` and `:468` mentions now say `system.txt` in the directory named by the JobSpec `custom_prompt_dir` field, and "JobSpec `custom_prompt_dir`".
+- **Stability tier sentence (extended, same file).** "`bare-review` is the only entry shipping `stable` ... All other 6 non-custom entries ship `experimental`" was wrong against code: `lenses/bare_review.py:71` and `lenses/reflect_review.py:71` both set `stability="stable"`; the other 6 set `"experimental"`. Rewritten to name both stable lenses; the tier table row "Default for entries beyond `bare-review`" became "Default for new entries".
+- **Out-of-item remnant left in place.** §6 and §8 say CI runs `superclaude swarm validate-lenses` through `make verify-sync` and that a local pre-commit hook runs it with `--warning-mode`. Neither is wired: `Makefile:166` `verify-sync` and `.pre-commit-config.yaml` contain no `validate-lenses` call. §6 "Wiring task" already says the wiring is a follow-up. Not named by B-W15 or gaps 62-63, so not edited.
